// "Unless" — the ENGLISH ORDER over the `MustPay` punisher ([CR#118.12a]):
// "[effect] unless [who] pays [cost]" is `MustPay { actor: who, cost,
// or_else: effect }`, exactly. Core keeps only the CR-family `MustPay`
// node; this macro is the render name the corpus's unless-order spellings
// (Mana Leak's "counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}",
// the upkeep-toll "sacrifice ~ unless you pay …") read and write through —
// the parser's counter/sacrifice emitters keep emitting `Unless(...)`
// invocations, which expand to `MustPay` at read time.
//
// Rendering rides the structural `MustPay` arm (which conjugates the payer
// verb — "unless you pay" / "unless its controller pays"); the template
// documents the surface order.
(
    name: "Unless",
    template: "${effect} unless ${who} pays ${unless}",
    kinds: [Effect],
    params: { "effect": Effect, "who": Default(Reference, You), "unless": Cost },
    body: MustPay(
        actor: Param(who),
        cost: [Splice(Param(unless))],
        or_else: Param(effect),
    ),
)
